# Files executed inside the Linux container keep LF on every checkout. With
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) `scripts/start.sh` would otherwise
# be checked out with CRLF, and an image built from that working copy dies at
# its entrypoint with `env: 'sh\r': No such file or directory`.
*.sh text eol=lf
backend/Dockerfile text eol=lf
